               <head>Afghan legislation, 1303 AS/1924-1925</head>
               <msContents>
                  <summary>Handwritten copies of the texts of <title>niẓām'nāmah</title>s, i.e. the
                     new legislation of Afghanistan, for the year 1303 shamsī/March 21 1924 – March
                     20 1925. The contents of this volume consist mainly of regulations on
                     procedural matters, listed mostly in tabular form on f. 2. </summary>
                  <msItem
                     class="http://lccn.loc.gov/sh96011775 http://lccn.loc.gov/sh85001521"
                     n="1" xml:id="Uk_Or_16918-item1">
                     <note>
                        <p>Manuscripts of this type were compiled for reference purposes by local
                           administrators, and later for archival purposes, although during the
                           period of Amān Allāh Khān’s rule (r. 1919-1929) a large number of <hi
                              rend="italic">niẓāmnāmah</hi>s were published as lithographed
                           booklets. Provincial authorities were obliged to maintain handwritten
                           volumes and to bring them to Kabul periodically for scrutiny. A stamped
                           official form on f. 1r, accompanied by one clear impression of the royal
                           seal and several poor ones, explains the rules and warns of a penalty of
                           ten years’ imprisonment for altering or rubbing out entries.
                           Consequently, all the emendations in this manuscript are made by drawing
                           a line through the error and writing the correct wording above. The
                           official responsible for the maintenance of this volume is named on both
                           forms as Shaykh <persName role="asn" key="person_f9032">‘Izzat Allāh
                           Khān.</persName></p>
                     </note>
                     <textLang mainLang="per">Persian </textLang>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <physDesc>
                  <objectDesc form="codex">
